    "homepage_text": "Bin-Bin Gao's homepage\nBin-Bin Gao（高斌斌）\nPh.D., Senior Researcher\nYouTu Lab,\nTencent\nLAMDA Group,\nNanjing University\nShenzhen 518057, China\nEmail:\ncsgaobb@gmail.com\nor\ngaobb@lamda.nju.edu.cn\nBiography\n|\nNews\n|\nSelected Publications\n|\nActivities\n|\nHome\nBiography\nI am a Senior Researcher at\nTencent YouTu Lab\nin Shenzhen (技术大咖, 2018).\nPreviously, I received my Ph.D. in\nNanjing University\nat\nLAMDA Group\n, \nled by Prof.\nZhi-Hua Zhou\n(Member of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, Fellow of the ACM, AAAI, AAAS, IEEE et al.), \nadvised by Prof.\nJianxin Wu\n(member of the Thousand Talents Plan). \nBefore that, I got my B.S. degree in applied mathematics in 2010, and received my M.S. degree in 2013 from\nSouthwest University\n. My research interests include computer vision and machine learning, especially visual recognition and deep learning. \nI have served as an\nArea Chair for NeurIPS 2024/2025\n, and\nICML 2025/2026\n.\nI have served as a reviewer (or PC member) for CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, ACCV, WACV, NeurIPS, ICML, AAAI, IJCAI, TIP, TKDE, TMI, TII, TNNLS, NN, PR etc.\nResearch\nMy current focus is developing\nsimple and general\n(more essential and practical) methods/models under various constraints, such as zero-shot, few-shot, long-tail, continual, unsupervised, and open-world for computer vision applications including visual inspection in intelligent manufacturing, medical image diagnosis, pests and diseases detection in agriculture, and science discovery.\nFew-Shot Learning\nImage Classification [\nECCV 22\n][\nIJCAI 23\n], Semantic Segmentation [\nTMM 22\n]\nObject Detection and Instance Segmentation [\nNeurIPS 22\n],\n      Object Counting [\nPR 24\n]\n🚀🚀Open-World Image Segmentation and Object Detection with Variety Prompts (text, box, or a combination of them)\nVision Anomaly Detection\nUnified AD [\nECCV 2024\n],\n      Fully Unsupervised AD [\nPR 25\n]\nUniversal AD \n      [\nNeurIPS 24\n],\n      [\nAAAI 26\n]\n      🚀🚀 [\nUniADet\n]\nBenchmarking AD \n      [\nCVPR 24\n]\n      [\nCVPR 25\n]\n      [\narXiv 25\n]\nFew-shot Anomaly Generation\n[ECCV 2024]\nMultimodal AD\n      [\nICLR 25\n]\nContinual Learning\nImage Classification [\nTMM 23\n],\n      Object Detection [\nAAAI 24\n],\n      Anomaly Detection [\nAAAI 24\n]\nGeneral Object Recognition\nMulti-Label Image Recognition [\nTIP 21\n],\n      Change Detection [\nPR 22\n]\nImage Segementation, Object Detection\nEarlier Works\nDeep Label Distribution Leaning \n    [\nTIP 17\n]  \n    [\nIJCAI 18\n]\nVisual (Image and Video) Representation \n    [\nAAAI 16\n]\nSupport Vector Machine \n    [\nICMLA 15\n]\n🔥🔥🔥If you have interests on above topics, please directly send me email to\ncsgaobb at gmail dot com\n, and\nremote cooperations are welcomed\n.\n🔥🔥🔥\nI am recruiting self-motivated interns in computer vision. If you are interested in, please directly send your CV to\nmy email danylgao at tencent dot com\n,\n[招聘JD]\n.\nNews\nNov. 20, 2025: 🎉🎉🎉 I am going to be serving as an\nArea Chair for ICML 2026\n.\nNov. 08, 2025: 🎉🎉🎉 A paper on Universal Vision Anomaly Detection is accepted by\nAAAI 2026\n(accept rate: 17.6%).\nOct. 26, 2025: 🎉🎉🎉 I am invited as a Keynote Speaker for the ADFM 2026 workshop at\nCVPR 2026\n.\nJul. 26, 2025: A paper on Multi-Modal Model for Low-Level Vision Tasks is accepted by\nBMVC 2025\n.\nJul. 06, 2025: A paper on Box-supervised Instance Segmentation is accepted by\nACMMM 2025\n.\nMay. 09, 2025: Attend CCIG 2025 and give a talk,\n\"Towards Unified and Universal Visual Anomaly Detection\"\n, Changsha, China.\nFeb. 27, 2025: A paper on anomaly detection benchmark is accepted by\nCVPR 2025\n.\nFeb. 21, 2025: I will attend\nCCIG 2025\n, Changsha, China.\nFeb. 17, 2025: I will be serving as an\nArea Chair for NeurIPS 2025\n.\nJan. 23, 2025: A paper on anomaly detection is accepted by\nICLR 2025\n.\nDec. 16, 2024: A paper on anomaly detection is accepted by\nPattern Recognition\n.\nDec. 15, 2024: I'm goi