    "homepage_text": "Mieradilijiang\nMieradilijiang\nPublications\nTalks & Presentation\nAcademic Service\nProjects\nWork Experience\nCV & Others\nMieradilijiang Maimaiti\nPh.D., Assoc. Prof., School of CS, Xinjiang University. Former NLP senior algorithm engineer at DAMO ACADEMY in Alibaba Group. Research Interest: NLP, ML, LLM.\nFollow\nUrumqi, Xinjiang, China\nEmail\nResearchGate\nGithub\nStackoverflow\nWeibo\nGoogle Scholar\nORCID\n🧑‍🎓 Biography\nDr. Mieradilijiang Maimaiti is currently an Associate Professor at the\nSchool of Computer Science\n,\nXinjiang University (XJU)\n.\nBefore that, he worked as Senior Algorithm Engineer for Natural Language Processing (NLP) at the\nLanguage Technology Lab\nin\nALIBABA DAMO ACADEMY\n. Previously, Mieradilijiang received his Ph.D. from the\nDepartment of Computer Science\nat\nTsinghua University (THU)\nunder the supervision of\nProf. Maosong Sun\nand is also co-advised by\nProf. Yang Liu\nin the\nTHUNLP Lab\n. His work focuses on NLP, machine translation (MT), and machine learning (ML). Mieradilijiang has been involved in MT-related work since September 2016, specifically concentrating on neural machine translation (NMT) involving low-resource languages (LRLs) and morphologically rich languages (MRLs), which include minority languages. Additionally, he has researched the domain adaptation problem in NMT and delved into transfer learning and data augmentation for LRLs in NMT. Concurrently, he has dedicated attention to morphological analysis in agglutinated and inflected languages.\nBefore joining\nTHUNLP Lab\n, he earned his master’s and bachelor’s degrees from the\nSchool of Information Science and Engineering\nat\nXinjiang University (XJU)\n, specializing in software engineering and computer science, respectively. Throughout his master’s program, he delved into computational morphology, speech recognition, speech synthesis, and morphological analysis under the guidance of academician\nProf. Wushouer Silamu\n. During his undergraduate studies, he developed various desktop applications, including educational software, medical applications, several network applications (for corporate and official government websites), and some valuable apps for Android and Windows Phone. Mieradilijiang gained experience in software development for desktop, network, and smart mobile devices before pursuing his Ph.D.\nFurthermore, he possesses a keen interest in leveraging ML to address various NLP issues. Presently, he continues to explore intriguing methodologies for Natural Language Generation, such as Machine Translation or automated content creation, and for Natural Language Understanding, including reasoning and semantic retrieval.\nNothing is impossible!\n🔎 Research Interests\nMieradilijiang has a broad research interest in language technology:\nNatural Language Processing\nMachine Translation\nLow-Resource Languages Scenario\nData Augmentation\nTransfer Learning\nDomain Adaptation\nPrior-Knowledge\nMorphological Analysis &\nWord Segmentation\nSemantic Representation\n: Sentence Retrieval / Knowledge Retrieval\nSentiment Classification: Few-Shot Learning & Zero-Shot Learning\nMultilingual Processing\nPre-trained Models\n(PTMs) & LLMs\nInformation Retrieval\nCross-Language Information Retrieval\nMachine Learning for NLP\nNLP Applications\n🗞️ Latest News\n23/10/2025\nALTA2025\nOne paper has been accepted by ALTA2025.\n03/10/2025\nRising Star Award\nI was honored with the 2025 ACM China Lanzhou Chapter Rising Star Award.\n08/23/2025\nPRCV2025\nThree papers have been accepted by PRCV2025.\n06/03/2025\nKBS2025\nOne paper has been accepted by KBS2025.\n04/03/2025\nAI for Medicine\nI was invited to give an academic talk at Westlake University on the power of AI for Medicine.\n📰 Previous News\nMore\n10/23/2024\nLLM+Tool Learning\nI was invited to give an academic talk at Xinjiang Changji University on Tool Learning for LLM.\n09/19/2024\nEMNLP2024\nOne paper has been accepted by EMNLP2024 findings.\n08/16/2024\nYouth Science Foundation2024\nThe 'Youth Science Foundation'\nproject\nhas been approved by NSFC.\n07/28/2024\nPRCV2024\nOne paper has been accepted by PRCV2024.\n06/25/2024\nArxiv2024\nWe have constructed a multi-lingual RE corpus for LLMs.\n05/15/2024\nFM104.6\nI have received an invitation from the broadcasting and TV station of Urumqi.\nFull Version\n,\nWeChat QR\n,\nPrevue\n,\nFinal\n,\nSocial Practice\n,\nSuggestions\n03/03/2024\nArxiv2024\nWe have optimized cross-lingual PTM for SR.\n02/16/2024\nArxiv2024\nWe have introduced a new method for LLM-based MT.\n11/22/2023\nLLM+MT\nI was invited to give an academic talk at Xinjiang Yili Normal University on LLM for MT.\n11/05/2023\nRA Funding2023\nThe 'Special Research Assistant Funding'\nproject\napproved by CAS.\n08/15/2023\nTC Project2023\nThe 'Tianchi Talent'\nproject\napproved by Xinjiang HRSS.\n08/13/2022\nCIKM2022\nOne paper has been accepted by CIKM2022.\n06/10/2022\nPoster Presentation\nfor NAACL2022 uploaded.\n04/10/2022\nNAACL2022\nOne paper has been accepted by NAACL2022.\n11/08/2021\nOral Presentation\nfor EMNLP2021 uploaded.\n08/26/2021\nEMNLP2021\nTwo papers accepted have been accepted by EMNLP2021.\n05/24/2021\nPhD Defense\nCompleted!\n🌍 Visitor Distribution\nSitemap\nFollow:\nGitHub\nFeed\n© 2026 Mieradilijiang Maimaiti. Powered by\nJekyll\n&\nAcademicPages\n, a fork of\nMinimal Mistakes\n.",
