e President of LiAuto), Xianpeng Lang (Vice President of LiAuto), Sheng Sun\n[Conference] IEEE ICRA'26.\nNAVSIM LeaderBoard\nMy first work conducted at LiAuto AutoDrive. We achieve the state-of-the-art on the NAVSIM benchmark.\nThe Better You Learn, The Smarter You Prune: Towards Efficient Vision-language-action Models via Differentiable Token Pruning\nTitong Jiang*\n,\nXuefeng Jiang*\n, Yuan Ma, Xin Wen, Bailin Li, Kun Zhan, Peng Jia, Yahui Liu, Sheng Sun, Xianpeng Lang\n[Conference]  IEEE ICRA'26.\nProject site\nMy first VLA model with open-sourced paper&codes&checkpoints which achieves new state-of-the-art performance on LIBERO. Thanks to friends and experts of LiAuto.\nRepresentation Optimal Matching for Federated Learning with Noisy Labels in Remote Sensing\nXuefeng Jiang\n, Tian Wen, Sheng Sun, Jinliang Yuan, Huashuo Liu, Lvhua Wu, Yuwei Wang and Min Liu\n[Journal]\nIEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing (IEEE TMC)\n, 2025\nIEEE early access version\nSpecial acknowledgement: FedRS dataset and its authors [Link]\nTackling Noisy Clients in Federated Learning with End-to-end Label Correction\nXuefeng Jiang\n, Sheng Sun, Jia Li, Jingjing Xue, Runhan Li, Zhiyuan Wu, Gang Xu, Yuwei Wang and Min Liu\n[Conference]\nACM International Conference on Information & Knowledge Managements (ACM CIKM)\n, 2024\narXiv\nTo refine the noisy labels of noisy clients via an end-to-end optimization framework in the scenario of distributed learning.\nTowards Federated Learning against Noisy Labels via Local Self-Regularization\nXuefeng Jiang\n, Sheng Sun, Yuwei Wang, Min Liu\n[Conference]\nACM International Conference on Information & Knowledge Managements (ACM CIKM)\n, 2022,\nNSF/SIGWeb student award\narXiv\nAn early attempt to deal with noisy labels considering privacy concern of Federated Learning.\nVIPS-Odom: Visual-Inertial Odometry Tightly-coupled with Parking Slots for Autonomous Parking\nXuefeng Jiang*\n,\nFangyuan Wang*\n,\nRongzhang Zheng*\n, Han Liu, Yixiong Huo, Jinzhang Pen