    "talking_points": "You lead the O Team at Zhipu AI focusing on Reasoning RL and Agentic RL for the GLM family—including GLM-4.5 and Z1—could you share how your team balances agentic autonomy with reliable reasoning guarantees?\nYour work spans both foundational RL infrastructure (e.g., slime, an open-source RL framework) and applied long-context modeling—how do you see these two threads converging in next-gen foundation models?\nWith deep expertise across knowledge graph reasoning (e.g., SQUIRE, FactE), interpretability evaluation (EMNLP 2021 benchmark), and scalable training techniques, how do you prioritize research directions that bridge theory, reliability, and real-world deployment?\nYou’ve contributed to major open-source tools like OpenKE and slime—what design principles guide your approach to building reusable, production-ready AI infrastructure?\nHaving trained under Prof. Juanzi Li at Tsinghua and published consistently across ACL, EMNLP, and arXiv on reasoning, KGs, and RL, how has your definition of 'reasoning-capable AI' evolved from your early KGC work to GLM-4.5’s hybrid thinking/direct-response architecture?",
