    "homepage_text": "Jingyu Xiao\nJingyu Xiao\nHome\nHome\nJingyu Xiao (肖劲宇), Whale\nPhD at CUHK; MS at Tsinghua University; BS at Wuhan University\njyxiao@link.cuhk.edu.hk;jy-xiao21@tsinghua.org.cn; whalexiao99@gmail.com (prefer);\n🐳 About Me\nI am a second-year Ph.D. student at\nThe Chinese University of Hong Kong\n, supervised by Prof.\nMichael R.Lyu\n(IEEE/ACM/AAAS Fellow), where I am supported by\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship (HKPFS)\n.\nI obtained my M.S. (2021-2024) in Computer Science at\nTsinghua University\nwith Outstanding Graduate Award, supervised by Professor\nYong Jiang\nand Professor\nQing Li\n.\nI received my Bachelor's degree (2017-2021) from\nWuhan University\n.\nMy research interests mainly include: (1) Large Language Models: Code Intelligence, AI Safety, GUI Agents. (2) Data Mining: User Behavior Modeling, Anomaly Detection, Recommendation and Graph Mining. (3) Computer Networks: Smart Homes, Network Failure Localization, Network Function Virtualization and Programmable Switches.\n🔥🔥The rapid advancements in generative AI, particular Multi-modal Large Language Models (MLLMs), now excelling in multimodal understanding and code generation. Recently, I mainly explore code intelligence of MLLMs in multimodal scenarios, e.g., UI code generation/repair, slide/chart/poster generation.\n🔥🔥I created\nAwesome-Multimodal-LLM-for-Code\nrepository and keep updating it. This is the first Awesome MLLM4Code repository and promotes code generation research under multi-modal scenarios. I also maintain the\nWebPAI (Web Development Powered by AI)\nproject, aiming to build an AI platform for more reliable and practical automated webpage generation.\nIf you find our work interesting, feel free to contact me for discussion or collaboration.\n🔥 News\n[2025.11]\n🎉🎉 SmartGen (project-lead) got accepted by SIGKDD 2026, see you in Jeju, South Korea🇰🇷!\n[2025.9]\n🎉🎉 Instruct4Edit (co-author) got accepted by AIWare 2025!\n[2025.8.21]\n🎉🎉 SlideCoder (co-first-author) got accepte