    "homepage_text": "Zhijian Ou @ Tsinghua University\nZhijian Ou - Professor, Department of Electronic Engineering, Tsinghua University\nHome\nTeaching\nResearch\nPaper\nSoftware\nNews\nTalk videos can be found\nhere\nat bilibili;\r\nCode\nhere\nat github; \r\nChinese blogs\nhere\nat zhihu; \r\nChinese news\nhere\nat weibo;\r\nEnglish news\nhere\nat X.\nGENERAL INFORMATION\nCurriculum Vitae\n2024.12 - present\nProfessor.\n2018.12 - present\nCo-founder and Chief Scientist of TasiTech.\n2008.12 - 2024.12\nAssociate professor.\n2014.08 - 2015.07\nVisiting Scholar, Beckman Institute, University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign.\n2003.08 - 2008.12\nAssistant professor, Department of Electronic Engineering, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China.\n1998.09 - 2003.07\nPh.D. in electronic engineering from Tsinghua University, Beijing, China.\n1994.09 - 1998.07\nB.S. with the highest honor in electronic engineering from Shanghai Jiaotong University, Shanghai, China.\nRESEARCH INTERESTS\nSpeech and Language Processing (particularly speech recognition and dialogue systems)\nMachine Intelligence (particularly with graphical models and deep learning)\nI'm broadly interested in\nDealing with Uncertainty for Intelligent Systems\n. The two fundamental problems are first to construct  probabilistic models of the studied phenomenon using human knowledge and machine learning algorithms, and second to find efficient ways of implementing probabilistic inference with those models. Graphical models have emerged as a general framework for describing and applying probabilistic models, while the core is probability theory and mathematical statistics.\nCurrent interests are\nSpeech and Language Processing\n, by proposing new models of speech and language, developing new methods for learning and inference with those models, and applying them to real tasks in speech and language processing. 100,000 years ago, humans started to speak so they could free up their hands. Is it going to happen again? Getting rid of keyboards and talking to machines is not a dream in the near future, I believe. Moreover, efficient searching, mining, and browsering the large amounts of digital media, in which speech is often an indispensable component, also needs speech signal and information processing techniques.\n人类智能本质是否在于能有效处理不确定性，这个问题还有待进一步研究论证。但处理不确定性是智能的一种重要表现――这个认识已经得到众多研究者的肯定和践行。我广泛感兴趣于\n智能系统中的不确定性处理――统计机器智能\n。这涉及两个基本问题，一是借助人类知识和机器学习算法，建立所研究对象的概率模型，二是基于建立的模型，寻找有效概率推理的方法。图模型已逐渐成为描述和应用概率模型的一般框架，其核心是概率论和数理统计。\n目前研究兴趣在\n语音信号与信息处理\n。语音处理是机器智能的一个重要切入点。十万年以前，人学会用言语进行交流，释放了双手，从猿进化到人，这是人类文明的重要一步。当今人类进入计算机广泛使用的信息时代，如何能让人的双手不再受键盘鼠标束缚，人与机器进行自然的言语人机交互？我相信，这在不久的将来不再是一个梦想，将带来人类文明的又一大进步。此外，音频是多媒体的不可缺少的一部分。对日益增多的音视频内容进行有效地搜索、挖掘和浏览，也非常需要语音信号与信息处理技术。\nRESEARCH PROJECTS\nPrincipal investigator\n: National Science Foundation China (NSFC), China governmental fundings, joint research with Intel, Panasonic, IBM, Toshiba, Apple, China Mobile, China Unicom, TasiTech, Meituan, etc.\nTEACHING\nGraduate courses\nTheory and Applications of Probabilistic Graphical Models, since  2004 Fall.\nUndergraduate courses\nProbability and Stochastic Processes (1), since 2012 Spring.\nProbability and Stochastic Processes (2), since 2012 Fall.\nMathematics and engineering applications, 2005 Spring - 2011 Spring.\nPROFESSIONAL ACTIVITIES\nIEEE Senior Member (2014-present)\nSenior Area Editor (01/2025-01/2028), Associate Editor (05/2019-05/2024), IEEE/ACM Transactions on Audio, Speech and Language Processing (T-ASLP)\nEditorial Board Member (11/2021-07/2025), Computer Speech and Language\nSenior Area Editor (03/2024-03/2026), IEEE Signal Processing Letters\nChair of Workshops Sub-Committee (since 2022) and Committee Member (2020 - 2022, 2023 - 2025), IEEE Speech and Language Processing Technical Committee (SLTC)\nCommittee Member (2019-present), APSIPA Machine Learning and Data Analytics (MLDA) Technical Committee\nDistinguished Member (2022-present), China Computer Federation (CCF)\nStanding Committee Member (2018-