    "talking_points": "Your Ph.D. research at Iowa State focuses on scalable multi-agent computational guidance for Urban Air Mobility using MDPs and Monte Carlo Tree Search — a compelling intersection of RL and aerospace systems.\nYou've contributed to high-impact publications in JGCD, AIAA Aviation, and NeurIPS workshops, especially on prioritized sequence experience replay and decentralized coordination for eVTOL traffic.\nYour industry experience spans applied ML at ByteDance and UTM/decision-system internships at Airbus A^3 and AirMap — giving you rare dual expertise in both cutting-edge AI and real-world aviation autonomy.\nYour background bridges applied mathematics (HIT B.S.) and aerospace engineering (ISU Ph.D.), with rigorous coursework in optimization, stochastic systems, and deep learning — ideal for safety-critical autonomous systems.\nYou built an OpenAI Gym-based free-flight airspace simulator with environment uncertainty — demonstrating strong engineering ability to translate theoretical RL/MDP work into validated, reproducible systems.",
