    "homepage_text": "Yushi Bai\nYushi Bai 白雨石\nI am a Fourth-year Ph.D. student at Tsinghua University, advised by Prof.\nJuanzi Li\n. I reveived my B.E. in\nYao class\nfrom Tsinghua University in 2022. I have been very fortunate to work with Prof.\nJie Tang\n, Prof.\nZhiyuan Liu\n, Prof.\nJure Leskovec\n, and Prof.\nAriel Procaccia\n.\nEmail\n/\nGoogle Scholar\n/\nGithub\n/\nNews\n/\nSelected Publications\n/\nExperience\n/\nHonors & Awards\nNews\n[2026.02]\nGLM-5 is released! Checkout the technical report\nhere\n. I am one of the core contributors, responsible for the new model arch (DSA), improvements, and RL adaptation.\n[2026.01]\nAwarded the first\nTencent Project Up Scholarship\n(15 recipients in total).\n[2026.01]\nLongWriter-Zero\naccepted to ICLR 2026 as Oral presentation!\n[2025.09]\nTwo papers accepted to NeurIPS 2025, including one Spotlight!\n[2025.05]\nThree papers including LongBench v2 accepted to ACL 2025! See you in Vienna!\nSelected Publications\nMy research interests primarily lie in large language models (LLMs), covering long-context LLM, LLM evaluation and safety, and multimodality. Recently, I have been focusing on designing more efficient and comprehensive LLM architectures that push beyond traditional architectures, particularly in long-context and agentic scenarios. Below are some of my lead works (see my\nGoogle Scholar\nfor a complete list).\nLong-Context LLM\n(6)\nLLM Evaluation & Safety\n(5)\nMultimodal\n(5)\nKnowledge Graph Reasoning\n(3)\nFair Division\n(2)\nLong-Context LLM\nLongWriter-Zero: Mastering Ultra-Long Text Generation via Reinforcement Learning\nYuhao Wu*,\nYushi Bai*\n,\n                      Zhiqiang Hu, Roy Ka-Wei Lee, Juanzi Li\nICLR 2026\n[\npaper\n]\n                      [\ncode\n]\nOral presentation (Top 5%)\nLongBench v2: Towards Deeper Understanding and Reasoning on Realistic Long-context Multitasks\nYushi Bai*\n,\n                      Shangqing Tu*, Jiajie Zhang, Hao Peng, Xiaozhi Wang, Xin Lv, Shulin Cao, Jiaz