    "homepage_text": "About | Kailiang Zhong\nKailiang Zhong\nAbout\nResume\nStats\nContact\n☰\nOpen Menu\nKailiang Zhong\nAbout\nResume\nStats\nContact\nClose Menu\nAbout Me\n(in about 605 words)\n简介｜Intro\n我是一个算法工程师，主要从事于 Uplift 建模、因果推断、推荐系统相关工作。现在在字节跳动（Bytedance）负责抖音支付用户增长/营销算法相关工作。 之前在阿里国际-Lazada 负责各类优惠券营销算法/用户定价，再之前在腾讯负责直播推荐。\n擅长各类场景、激励、用户生命周期的 Uplift 建模、运筹决策以及相应的营销算法工作。\n论文发表\n：SIGKDD（简称 KDD）2022《\nDESCN\n: Deep Entire Space Cross Networks for Individual Treatment Effect\n》（一作）\n专利\n: 《\n基于 LPA 算法对主播进行反作弊识别\n》\n页面中出现的二维码是我的个人公众号：BR 的纸飞机。平时会分享一些技术文章和思考在\n公众号\n和\n知乎\n，欢迎朋友们一起交流学习。\n技术博客\n，欢迎交流｜合作。\n[English Version]\nI am an\nAlgorithm Engineer\nspecializing in\nUplift Modeling, Causal Inference, and Recommender Systems\n. Currently, I work at\nByteDance\n, where I focus on user growth and marketing algorithms for\nDouyin Pay\n. My professional background includes developing incentive and pricing algorithms at\nAlibaba (Lazada)\nand building live-streaming recommendation systems at\nTencent\n.\nI have extensive experience in Uplift modeling, operations research, and marketing strategy optimization across various business scenarios and user life cycles.\nPublication\n: First author of the SIGKDD '22 paper:\nDESCN\n: Deep Entire Space Cross Networks for Individual Treatment Effect\n.\nTech Blog\n: I share my technical insights on\nZhihu\n. Feel free to reach out for collaboration or professional exchange!\n一些故事｜Some Stories\n关于我是如何入门机器学习\n：在 2013 年的时候，由于某种契机，我接触到了\nCoursera\n并且学习了台湾大学\n林轩田教授\n的两门课程\n《机器学习基石》\n和\n《机器学习技法》\n。当时我大三，这两门课程对我来说相当有挑战性。庆幸的是，我遇到了一位名叫\nBeader\n的网友，他当时在台湾读研，也在学习这两门课。Beader 经常鼓励我并与我讨论作业，让我能够坚持下来并最终拿到了结业证书。后来，我们一起参加了 Kaggle 的 PAKDD 比赛（获得 Top 5%）以及\n2014 年阿里巴巴第一届天池大数据竞赛\n（在 7,000 多支队伍中排名第 78）。当时我们队有三个人，另一位是他的女同学。后来，他们在一起了，再后来，他们结婚了：）\nHow I Got Started with Machine Learning\n: Back in 2013, I stumbled upon Coursera and took two foundational courses by Professor Hsuan-Tien Lin from National Taiwan University:\nMachine Learning Foundations\nand\nMachine Learning Techniques\n. During my third year of university, I found the material quite challenging. Fortunately, I met a fellow learner online named\nBeader\n, who was a graduate student in Taiwan at the time. Beader encouraged me and we frequently discussed assignments, which helped me stay on track and eventually earn my certificates. Later, we teamed up for the PAKDD competition on Kaggle (ranking in the top 5%) and the\n1st Alibaba Tianchi Big Data Competition\nin 2014, where we ranked 78th out of over 7,000 teams. Our third teammate was his classmate—she later became his girlfriend, and eventually, his wife. :)\n2015 年参加了第二届阿里天池大数据竞赛——“阿里移动推荐算法”，队名 Wonder，排名 37/7186。\nIn 2015\n, I participated in the\n2nd Alibaba Tianchi Big Data Competition (Mobile Recommendation)\n. Our team, \"Wonder,\" ranked\n37th out of 7,186\nteams.\n2019 年去了新疆环天山山脉自驾，在安集海大峡谷看过如水彩画般的河谷，在独库公路一日历经四季。风景极美，我以后还会再去。如果你还没去过，我强烈推荐你去看看。当然，还有那拉提草原、赛里木湖。\nIn 2019\n, I went on a self-driving trip around the\nTianshan Mountains in Xinjiang\n. I witnessed the watercolor-like riverbeds of the Anjihai Grand Canyon and experienced all four seasons in a single day along the\nDuku Highway\n. The scenery was breathtaking, and I definitely plan to return in the future. If you haven't been there, I highly recommend visiting—especially places like the\nNalati Grassland\nand\nSayram Lake\n.\n2020 年春节前夕（新冠疫情爆发前夕），带爸妈去了新加坡和马来西亚。我们在马六甲度过了除夕，这也是我和爸妈第一次在国外过年，留下了非常美好的回忆。\nFor the 2020 Lunar New Year\n(just before the COVID-19 outbreak), I took my parents on a trip to\nSingapore and Malaysia\n. We spent New Year's Eve in Malacca. It was the first time any of us had celebrated the New Year abroad, and it remains one of our most cherished memories.\n2020 年国庆自驾川西大环线，走了 317、318 国道，熊猫大道，去了理塘、稻城亚丁。 深夜赶路去稻城时，在一处山路停留休息，我看到了 0 光污染下的清澈银河，抬头一瞬间还以为自己置身于太空。\nDuring the 2020 National Day holiday\n, I embarked on a grand loop road trip through\nWestern Sichuan\n, traversing National Highways 317 and 318, as well as the Panda Avenue, visiting\nLitang\nand\nDaocheng Yading\n. While driving deep into the night toward Daocheng, I pulled over on a mountain pass to rest. Under zero light pollution, I was met with a breathtakingly clear view of the Milky Way. For a split second, looking up made me feel as though I were drifting in outer space.\n现在在练习英文口语中，欢迎同志一起交流学习，有好的资源或方法也欢迎推荐，不甚感激。\nCurrently, I am practicing my spoken English.\nI would love to connect with anyone interested in language exchange. If you have any great resources or tips to share, I would be deeply grateful!\n爱好｜Interests\nRunning & Swimming\nWriting\n: Sharing thoughts on\nZhihu\nMusic & Photography\n去过的地方｜Travels\nOriginally from\nGuangdong, China\n.\n2020\n: Singapore, Malaysia, Western Sichuan.\n2019\n: Xinjiang (Tianshan Loop).\n2018\n: Thailand.\n诗和远方｜Vision\nTo always find inspiration.\nTo enable a brighter future through technology.\nTo keep evolving and doing better.\n友情链接｜Links\nBeader Chen\n— My friend and mentor from the early days of my ML journey.\nDugang Liu\nKailiang Zhong（钟锴亮）\nbrice.zhong@gmail.com\nAbout\nI am an Algorithm Engineer at ByteDance,\nwith a focus on causal inference and uplift modeling\nLearn More\n© Kailiang D'Zhong\nlemoner.me\n.",
